    description: "Concept audit 2026-10-21/22 (pinned dev e9215548f6; write-up ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept_audit_10212026/concept-audit-vocabulary-since-0923_10222026.md). F3. Verified through the production CLI on devref e9215548f6: lib.py 'def build_registry(): ...; REGISTRY = build_registry(); def run(): return REGISTRY' imported by main.py (if __name__ == '__main__': lib.run()) -> 'dead-code-maybe --seeds entrypoints' reports build_registry dead (it runs at import). Default --seeds production hides it (exported API seeded). Agent probe (not re-checked): test_only_reachability.py:268-289 (any src in a test path is a test caller) vs dead-code's test bucket cli.py:9395 and sketch coverage sketch.py:5345 (function/method seeds only) disagree on one fixture (CASES = build_cases() at test-module level; a test-class-body call). Fix shape: an anchor is reached when its container is (file: imported/executed; class body: its module imported; Java static init: class used; field initializer: class constructed), one shared rule for all three consumers."  # 4cea
